✓ The dpop_jkt authorization request parameter binds the authorization code to the client's DPoP public key by conveying its JWK Thumbprint.
  RFC9449 §10 ¶1

✗ The client includes the dpop_jkt parameter in the authorization request with the JWK Thumbprint of its DPoP public key.
  struck: quote-not-found

✓ At the token endpoint, the authorization server verifies that the JWK Thumbprint of the DPoP proof's public key matches the dpop_jkt value and must reject the request if they differ.
  RFC9449 §10 ¶2

✓ This binding prevents an attacker from using a captured authorization code with a different DPoP key.
  RFC9449 §11.9 ¶1

✓ The dpop_jkt parameter is optional and can be combined with PKCE for additional security.
  RFC9449 §10 ¶6

